.TH std::ctype 3 "2026.11.10" "http://cppreference.com" "C++ Standard Libary"
.SH NAME
std::ctype \- std::ctype

.SH Synopsis
Defined in header <locale>
template<>
class ctype<char>;

This specialization of std::ctype encapsulates character classification features for type
char. Unlike general-purpose std::ctype, which uses virtual functions, this specialization
uses table lookup to classify characters (which is generally faster).

The base class std::ctype<char> implements character classification equivalent to the
minimal "C" locale. The classification rules can be extended or modified if constructed
with a non-default classification table argument, if constructed as
std::ctype_byname<char> or as a user-defined derived facet. All std::istream formatted
input functions are required to use std::ctype<char> for character classing during input
parsing.

